	"note": "Per runtime key (Bun by minor, Node by major) and e2e build cell: the cell's build time over a honey-free reference build's (packages/core/tests/e2e/build-gate.ts), from the RATIO build lines of the build and prod e2e jobs of CI runs 41387936376, 41390520719, 41392173897, 41394043578, 41395774324, 41397685122, 41399625780, 41401699590, 41403589880, 41405437361, 41406713265, 41408712784 (ci.yml dispatched with build_mode=record). Each job is classed fast, middle or slow by its own surface builds on bun, Node-only jobs unclassified; byClass is each class's median. baseline: the median of every job's ratio. ceiling (build-gate.ts ceilingRule): per cell, fit log(ratio) (mean m, sample sd s), sigma_upper = s * sqrt((n-1)/chi2_0.10,n-1) (one-sided 90% upper bound on sigma), z = Phi^-1(1 - 0.02/G) with G = 42 cells, ceiling = max(worst x 1.10, exp(m + z*sigma_upper)), so the cells share a 2% per-run false-red budget. A ratio above its ceiling is REGRESSED. catches: ceiling / baseline. No retry: a red with honey unchanged is answered by a re-record (6+ runs spanning both runner classes, derived by derive-build-ceilings.ts), never a rerun. Derived --by-commit: a cell whose head-commit groups agree (each group's median within the other's range, per runner class) pools them; any other takes the newest commit's runs alone.",
